{%- comment -%}
  The platform bento, its detail accordion, and the video lightbox those tiles open.

  Split out of tonescan-landing so the page composes from real sections in a JSON
  template. Page-wide CSS and JS are rendered once by layout/tonescan.liquid, so this
  file carries markup only and can be reordered or removed without taking them with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tonescan-landing tw:text-neutral-200">
  {%- comment -%} Screenshots live in Shopify Files (Content > Files). {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ts_cdn = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0634/3199/9736/files' -%}

  <section id="features" class="tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:scroll-mt-[84px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[760px] tw:text-center">
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">
        Everything a film scan needs
      </h2>
      <p class="tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[18px] tw:max-w-[720px] tw:text-[17px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-neutral-400">
        Capture, calibration, conversion, culling and export.<br class="tw:hidden tw:md:inline">
        A complete suite built for film photographers.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      HEADLINE FEATURES, these nine, in this order, are the ones the page leads on. Anything
      that isn't one of them belongs in the "Plus everything" list below, not here.
      Every tile carries a "+" that opens a short video of the feature (.ts-feature-more):
        data-video  = mp4 URL. EMPTY FOR NOW, the modal falls back to the poster plus a
                      "video coming soon" line, so tiles stay clickable until the clips exist.
        data-poster = still shown before playback / instead of it
        data-title  = heading inside the modal
      Filling in data-video is the only change needed when a clip is ready.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Nine cards, two of them large. Placement is explicit per position in the CSS below, so
      SOURCE ORDER IS VISUAL ORDER, move an <article> and update its nth-child rule together.
        1 engine (2x2)  2 RGB        3 GPU viewport
        4 flat-field    5 batch edit 6 speed (2x2)
        7 standalone    8 auto-crop  9 hardware control
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ts-bento-grid tw:mt-[48px]">
      <article class="ts-bento ts-bento--lg">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/pixel-preview.png" data-title="Rich inversion engine" aria-label="Watch: Rich inversion engine"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="ts-bento__media">
          <div class="ts-shot">
            <img src="{{ ts_cdn }}/pixel-preview.png" alt="A converted frame beside the live RGB histogram and the develop controls" loading="lazy" width="3200" height="2000">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ts-bento__text">
          <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="1"/><path d="M4 20c5 0 4-6 8-6s4-8 8-8"/><circle cx="9.4" cy="15.2" r="1.1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/><circle cx="14.6" cy="8.8" r="1.1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="tw:text-[22px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Rich inversion engine</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[10px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">Rendering modelled on real film physics and the way darkroom paper responds to light. The starting point already looks like a print, so you are adjusting to taste rather than rescuing a file.</p>
          <a class="ts-bento__cta" href="#gallery">See samples <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h9M8.5 4l4 4-4 4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/rgb-merge.png" data-title="Seamless RGB scanning" aria-label="Watch: Seamless RGB scanning"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/rgb-merge.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="9.5" r="5"/><circle cx="15" cy="9.5" r="5"/><circle cx="12" cy="15" r="5"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Seamless RGB scanning</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Trichromatic capture from any camera, mono sensors included. Triplets merged for you.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/pixel-preview.png" data-title="GPU viewport, 1:1 previews" aria-label="Watch: GPU viewport, 1:1 previews"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/pixel-preview.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 4h18v13H3z"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4M6 13l3.5-4 2.5 3 2-2.5L20 13"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">GPU viewport, 1:1 previews</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Every slider lands on a full-resolution preview instantly. No proxy, no wait.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/develop.png" data-title="Flat-field correction" aria-label="Watch: Flat-field correction"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/develop.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="6" ry="4"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Flat-field correction</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Cancels uneven light and lens falloff, so corners match the centre.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/organise.png" data-title="Batch editing" aria-label="Watch: Batch editing"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/organise.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 9a8 8 0 0 1 13.5-4.5L20 7M20 15a8 8 0 0 1-13.5 4.5L4 17"/><path d="M20 3v4h-4M4 21v-4h4"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Batch editing</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Get one frame right and the whole roll follows, matched from first frame to last.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento ts-bento--lg">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/batch-export.png" data-title="Properly fast" aria-label="Watch: Properly fast"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <div class="ts-bento__media">
          <div class="ts-shot">
            <img src="{{ ts_cdn }}/batch-export.png" alt="Exporting sixteen selected frames at once while the roll stays browsable" loading="lazy" width="3200" height="2000">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ts-bento__text">
          <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7z"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="tw:text-[22px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Properly fast</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[10px] tw:text-[15px] tw:leading-[1.55] tw:text-neutral-400">Smooth, instant previews of every edit, and a keyboard shortcut for everything so you can fly through a roll. Whole rolls convert and export in the background while you carry on working.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/organise.png" data-title="Standalone software" aria-label="Watch: Standalone software"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/organise.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16"/><path d="M3 9h18M6.5 6.5h.01M9 6.5h.01"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Standalone software</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">No Lightroom, no plugins, no host app. One program you own.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/develop.png" data-title="Smart auto-crop" aria-label="Watch: Smart auto-crop"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/develop.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 2v16h16M2 6h16v16"/><path d="M19.2 2.6l.6 1.6 1.6.6-1.6.6-.6 1.6-.6-1.6-1.6-.6 1.6-.6z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Smart auto-crop</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Frame edges found and squared up for you, on every shot.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="ts-bento">
        <button type="button" class="ts-feature-more" data-video="" data-poster="{{ ts_cdn }}/calibration-crosstalk.png" data-title="Hardware control" aria-label="Watch: Hardware control"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
        <span class="ts-bento__bg" style="--bg:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/calibration-crosstalk.png')" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ts-tile-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v3M12 18v3M3 12h3M18 12h3M5.6 5.6l2.1 2.1M16.3 16.3l2.1 2.1M18.4 5.6l-2.1 2.1M7.7 16.3l-2.1 2.1"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.4"/></svg></div>
        <div class="tw:mt-auto">
          <h3 class="tw:text-[17px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Hardware control</h3>
          <p class="tw:mt-[6px] tw:text-[14px] tw:leading-[1.5] tw:text-neutral-400">Drives your light source and advances the film carrier as you shoot.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      SECONDARY features, everything that is NOT one of the headline tiles above.
      Shown ONE GROUP AT A TIME behind tabs: as a single flat grid this ran to ~30 items and
      read as a wall. Panels are stacked in one grid cell and crossfaded, same pattern as the
      hero selector, so the block height doesn't jump between tabs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ts-more tw:mt-[64px] tw:md:mt-[88px]">
      <h3 class="tw:mb-[28px] tw:text-center tw:text-[20px] tw:font-semibold tw:text-white">Plus everything a serious workflow needs</h3>

      <div class="ts-more__acc">
        <div class="ts-more__item is-open" data-i="0">
          <button type="button" class="ts-more__trigger" aria-expanded="true">
            <span class="ts-more__cat">
              <span class="ts-more__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 7h3.5l1.5-2h8l1.5 2H21v12H3z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12.5" r="3.6"/></svg></span>Capture &amp; calibration
            </span>
            <span class="ts-more__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="ts-more__panel">
            <div class="ts-more__panelinner">
              <ul class="ts-morelist">
                <li><b>Hardware control</b>: drives your light source and advances the film carrier</li>
                <li><b>Tethered capture</b> straight into the current roll</li>
                <li><b>Light presets</b> read from a connected light</li>
                <li><b>Scan profiles</b>: calibrate once, reuse on every roll</li>
                <li><b>Per-channel exposure targets</b> with an EV meter</li>
                <li><b>Crosstalk correction</b> measured from your own setup</li>
                <li><b>Linearity calibration</b></li>
                <li><b>White-light scanning</b>: single-shot works too</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-more__item" data-i="1">
          <button type="button" class="ts-more__trigger" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="ts-more__cat">
              <span class="ts-more__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 6.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4.5 5H9l2 2.5h8.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 21 9v9.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 19.5 20h-15A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 18.5z"/></svg></span>Project management
            </span>
            <span class="ts-more__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="ts-more__panel">
            <div class="ts-more__panelinner">
              <ul class="ts-morelist">
                <li><b>Roll-based library</b> with live frame counts</li>
                <li><b>Watch folders</b> that ingest new scans as they land</li>
                <li><b>Automatic triplet detection</b> and merge</li>
                <li><b>Markers and colour labels</b> for fast culling</li>
                <li><b>Per-channel inspection</b>: view R, G or B alone</li>
                <li><b>Undo and redo</b> throughout</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-more__item" data-i="2">
          <button type="button" class="ts-more__trigger" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="ts-more__cat">
              <span class="ts-more__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 7h9M17 7h3M4 12h3M11 12h9M4 17h9M17 17h3"/><circle cx="15" cy="7" r="2"/><circle cx="9" cy="12" r="2"/><circle cx="15" cy="17" r="2"/></svg></span>Rich editing experience
            </span>
            <span class="ts-more__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="ts-more__panel">
            <div class="ts-more__panelinner">
              <ul class="ts-morelist">
                <li><b>Three process modes</b>: colour negative, B&amp;W negative, slide</li>
                <li><b>Live RGB histogram</b></li>
                <li><b>Exposure, contrast, density,</b> highlight rolloff and shadow lift</li>
                <li><b>Auto density</b></li>
                <li><b>Smart auto white balance</b>, or pick your own neutral</li>
                <li><b>Levels, tone trims and sharpening</b></li>
                <li><b>Crop, rotate and flip</b></li>
                <li><b>Pixel loupe</b> with a live density readout</li>
                <li><b>True exposure from raw</b>: read from signal, not the histogram</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-more__item" data-i="3">
          <button type="button" class="ts-more__trigger" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="ts-more__cat">
              <span class="ts-more__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3v11M8 10.5l4 4 4-4"/><path d="M4 16v3.5h16V16"/></svg></span>Professional exports
            </span>
            <span class="ts-more__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="ts-more__panel">
            <div class="ts-more__panelinner">
              <ul class="ts-morelist">
                <li><b>Colour-managed viewport and export</b>: sRGB, Adobe RGB, Display-P3 or Rec.2020, with the matching ICC profile embedded on the way out</li>
                <li><b>TIFF or JPG</b>, your quality and long edge</li>
                <li><b>Cineon log export</b> for grading downstream</li>
                <li><b>Filename patterns</b> from name, date, project or sequence</li>
                <li><b>Batch export</b> a selection or a whole roll</li>
                <li><b>Rich metadata</b>: film stock, camera and dev info on every file</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-more__item" data-i="4">
          <button type="button" class="ts-more__trigger" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="ts-more__cat">
              <span class="ts-more__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="1"/><path d="M3 9h18M6.5 6.5h.01M9 6.5h.01"/></svg></span>Platform
            </span>
            <span class="ts-more__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="ts-more__panel">
            <div class="ts-more__panelinner">
              <ul class="ts-morelist">
                <li><b>macOS and Windows</b>: native builds for both</li>
                <li><b>Keyboard-driven</b>: shortcuts for everything</li>
                <li><b>Fully standalone</b>: no host app, no plugin bridge</li>
                <li><b>Flexible licensing</b>: own it outright or subscribe</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="ts-vid" hidden>
    <div class="ts-vid__backdrop" data-close></div>
    <div class="ts-vid__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Feature video">
      <button class="ts-vid__close" type="button" aria-label="Close" data-close>&times;</button>
      <div class="ts-vid__stage"></div>
      <p class="ts-vid__title"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "toneScan features",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "toneScan features"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
